From: sdd-harness P2_4 worker <delivery-foundation-rearchitecture>
Subject: [PATCH 0005] comet 0.5.0: Kt knowledge-closeout blocks resolver completion (ADR-0022 B1)
Date: 2026-10-26  revision 2026-10-26-comet-050-adoption-v1

Purpose (ADR-0022, decision B1 — the ONLY patch kept on the 0.5.0 baseline):
Comet 0.5.0 has no post-archive hook (the resolver goes archived -> completed
unconditionally, and the composition factory rejects post-archive extensions),
so the managed-delivery Kt gate cannot be expressed as a composition
extension. This minimal successor of the retired 0003 patch restores the
Knowledge.Closeout.v1 semantic at the single seam that decides overall
completion:

  - Kp (project knowledge) stays a composition extension at
    full.verify.check.evidence and is re-verified by the upstream
    archive-time validateOutcome inside the archive directory;
  - Kt (team knowledge) MAY resume AFTER the archive move, on the SAME Run:
    while the obligation is pending, the resolver parks the run at
    <profile>.archive.execute instead of reporting 'completed'; once the
    closeout completes on that same Run, the resolver reports completion.

Predicate semantics — fail-open default, managed opt-in only:
  knowledgeCloseoutBlocked(classic) reads the OPTIONAL `knowledgeCloseout`
  field ({ required?: boolean; completed?: boolean } | null) from the
  ClassicState object given to the resolver. Absent/null (every upstream and
  legacy state) returns false, i.e. the previous unconditional completion is
  preserved byte-for-byte in behavior. The predicate blocks ONLY when
  required === true && completed !== true.

Explicit boundary (do not read more into this patch than it does):
  - ONLY domains/comet-classic/classic-resolver.ts is touched. The WRITE path
    that puts `knowledgeCloseout` onto the state (state-file wire keys, the
    managed admission that records the closeout) is NOT part of this patch;
    it belongs to the supply/admission wave (P1_3 adapter wiring) — this file
    pins the read-side semantic and its default-open behavior only.
  - Applying this patch (tools/comet supply step: upstream.lock.json
    patches[] + rebuild) is NOT done by P2_4; P2_4 ships the patch file and
    unit-verifies applicability + semantics against the pristine tree at
    .sdd/vendor/comet/aeb1a6598034e28ce46b8422d4dbd8785e607bd7/pristine.
  - <profile>.archive.execute is an EXISTING package step; parking there is
    non-destructive (the archive command reports the already-archived
    projection instead of re-archiving).

Verified by: test/delivery-cases/2_4.mjs (git apply --check + apply against a
pristine copy, target-line presence, and predicate truth-table evaluation on
the patched source).

diff --git a/domains/comet-classic/classic-resolver.ts b/domains/comet-classic/classic-resolver.ts
index 0b274c706f375b6e1f811ff821d41988fa95f063..55e900b7e8a851f573ebb55d316963a125b56a66 100644
--- a/domains/comet-classic/classic-resolver.ts
+++ b/domains/comet-classic/classic-resolver.ts
@@ -70,6 +70,25 @@ function resolveArchive(profile: ClassicProfile, classic: ClassicState): string
     : `${profile}.archive.confirm`;
 }
 
+// [sdd-harness 0005 / ADR-0022 decision B1] Optional managed-delivery
+// knowledge-closeout obligation (Knowledge.Closeout.v1: Kt may resume after
+// archive in the SAME Run and is required before overall completion). The
+// field is supplied by the managed host layer on the in-memory ClassicState;
+// upstream and legacy states never carry it, so an absent or null value keeps
+// the original resolver behavior exactly (fail-open default).
+interface KnowledgeCloseoutObligation {
+  required?: boolean;
+  completed?: boolean;
+}
+
+function knowledgeCloseoutBlocked(classic: ClassicState): boolean {
+  const closeout = (classic as ClassicState & {
+    knowledgeCloseout?: KnowledgeCloseoutObligation | null;
+  }).knowledgeCloseout;
+  if (closeout === null || closeout === undefined) return false;
+  return closeout.required === true && closeout.completed !== true;
+}
+
 export function resolveClassicStepId(
   classic: ClassicState,
   evidence: readonly ClassicEvidence[],
@@ -79,7 +98,16 @@ export function resolveClassicStepId(
   if (classic.archived && classic.phase !== 'archive') {
     throw new Error('archived=true requires phase=archive');
   }
-  if (classic.archived) return 'completed';
+  if (classic.archived) {
+    // [sdd-harness 0005 / ADR-0022 decision B1] Kt gate: an archived managed
+    // run whose knowledge closeout obligation is still pending stays on the
+    // SAME Run parked at the archive step instead of resolving 'completed';
+    // the closeout completes on this Run and only then does the resolver
+    // report completion. States without the optional field (all upstream
+    // states) keep the previous unconditional completion.
+    if (knowledgeCloseoutBlocked(classic)) return `${profile}.archive.execute`;
+    return 'completed';
+  }
   if (profile !== 'full' && classic.phase === 'design') {
     throw new Error(`${profile} workflow cannot enter design`);
   }
